    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green. `AcceptanceTest` (the only concrete test class; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper) passes both cases: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `locality`, a read-only field on the owner resource derived from `city` via the fixed table Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD (else `UNKNOWN`).\n\nFollowing the existing pattern for derived read-only fields (`membershipTier`, `membershipNumber`), I did it purely on read \u2014 no entity/DB change needed since it's a pure function of `city`:\n\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `locality` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n- **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(locality(owner))\")` and a `locality(Owner)` default method implementing the city\u2192region lookup (case-sensitive exact match, matching the test's `CITY_REGION` ground truth, and returning `UNKNOWN` for absent/unlisted cities).\n\nThe tests exercise the two spec branches \u2014 `POST /api/owners` with `city: \"Sydney\"` reads back `locality: \"NSW\"`, and a random unlisted city reads back `\"UNKNOWN\"` \u2014 both pass.",
